{
  "id": "COMPOUND:39670 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Benzyl Salicylate is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Benzyl Salicylate acts as a target of multiple compounds, including Armepavine, romidepsin, and Kolavenic Acid, all of which are linked to the High-affinity choline transporter. This indicates a potential mechanism where Benzyl Salicylate may influence the activity of these compounds, which in turn modulate the choline transporter. The shared relationship between Benzyl Salicylate and the choline transporter implies a possible role in cellular processes involving choline transport, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the biological network and underscores the importance of understanding how different compounds interact to regulate critical cellular functions.",
